{
  "$comment": "Herald seat permission profile. APPLIED 2026-08-05 by edict into the CIVILIZATION LAYER (civ/), not Manyhalls: the Herald was always civ-scope, his only input being the civilization digest across all forts. Paths repointed from fort/ to civ/ per docs/proposals/herald-founding/CIV-LAYER-SUPERSESSION.md. Publishing is covenant gate 6.1, unamendable. Modeled on warden-settings.json; loaded by civ/scripts/herald.sh with --setting-sources '' so this file is the ONLY permission source. Layering: this profile is policy, the kernel mask is the boundary. Verified caveat, same as every profile here: absent commands are not reliably denied, and deny rules bind a command SPELLING rather than a file (ForgeOs-21f.8, measured six-for-six). Treat allow as convenience, deny as intent, the mask as the boundary. The Herald reads the digest and writes prose; he has no reason to touch git, npm, or bd mutations, so all are denied. The fort/ deny rules are retained deliberately: he may not write a settlement's constitution either. AMENDED (fortkit-izz.2 round 2, 2026-08-07): the broad Edit(//home/justin/dev/**) deny shadowed the civ/handoffs fallback allow — deny beats allow, and Edit-family rules govern the Write tool, so his one repo write surface was unreachable (found by smoke probe 9). Replaced with enumerated protected surfaces: src, both constitutions (charter/seats/profiles/covenant), both launcher dirs (fort/scripts, civ/scripts), and his own law (civ/law) — a seat does not amend its own law. Every deny here restates what the kernel mask already enforces; the enumeration exists so intent stays readable without shadowing the fallback.",
